Spec: Native Keystore FRP bridge verification

Purpose:
  Exercise the actual packaged Android child and private bridge against a source-built authenticated backend.

Owns:
  ./FrpOwnerTest.java

Must:
  Keep all fixture configuration in target-private files and preserve nonexportable Keystore identity.
  Reject an unrelated same-UID socket client and verify actual frpc relay, inner peer mTLS, current server lease, large business bytes, half-close and server/local revocation.
  Bound the fixture and clean owned profile/socket/processes; do not add instrumentation administration to production Binder or owner interfaces.

  Report guest hold duration separately from coordinator-measured server-trigger-to-close time; only the latter verifies the five-second revocation deadline.
